  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "The stem is only the target word, with no other words around it.",
      "Use a two-syllable word that ends in le and has at least five letters.",
      "Give four choices. Each one is that word with a single hyphen, and the letters stay in order.",
      "The right split starts the last part at the letter just before le. If that letter is written twice, split between the pair.",
      "Use explain_key double_cle when that letter is doubled. Examples are ap-ple, lit-tle, bub-ble, mid-dle, and puz-zle.",
      "Use explain_key single_cle when that letter is not doubled. Examples are ta-ble, tur-tle, can-dle, ea-gle, ti-tle, cir-cle, peo-ple, and sin-gle.",
      "Wrong choices only slide the hyphen. Include a cut that pulls l away from e, and do not invent a new spelling.",
      "Tier 1 words show an easy doubled letter. Tier 3 wrong cuts sit one letter away, as in eag-le, tit-le, peop-le, cast-le, and whist-le.",
      "Do not use three or more syllables, ck before le, plurals, sound symbols, slashes, or phoneme clips.",
      "Set media to one lemma, the stem word. Do not describe a picture or invent an audio file.",
      "Keep words in school, home, food, pets, play, family, or weather. No brands and no real names.",
      "Use each stem word once before repeating one, and do not park the right split in the same slot every time."
    ]
  },
